      "description": "Watch Bolton Wanderers vs Lincoln highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. Championship Intensity at Bolton On August 29, 2026 , Bolton Wanderers hosted Lincoln City in a highly anticipated Championship fixture. Both teams entered the pitch looking to assert their dominance in a league known for its relentless pace and physical demands, setting the stage for a tactical battle from the opening whistle. Tactical Stalemate in the First Half The opening period was characterized by disciplined defending and a crowded midfield. Neither side was willing to concede ground easily, leading to a match of fine margins. The competitive nature of the contest was highlighted in the 31st minute when Ben House received a yellow card for a robust challenge. Despite flashes of creativity from both wings, clear-cut chances remained elusive, and the referee brought the first half to a close with the scoreline still deadlocked at 0-0. The Breakthrough Moment As the second half commenced, the energy levels rose significantly. Both managers turned to their benches around the hour mark to find a spark; Bolton introduced Kyliane Dong and Gaizka Larrazabal , while Lincoln brought on Robert Street . The deadlock was finally broken in the 66th minute. Callum Elder delivered a pinpoint assist into the path of Ben House , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net to give Lincoln City a 1-0 lead. It was a clinical finish that rewarded the visitors' persistence. Late Drama and Defensive Resilience Trailing by a goal, Bolton Wanderers threw everything forward in the closing stages. The introduction of Ryan Hardie and Jayden Nelson injected fresh pace into their attack, but Lincoln’s defense held firm. The game grew increasingly heated as Ivan Varfolomeev and Conor McGrandles both entered the referee's book for tactical fouls. Despite six minutes of added time and relentless pressure from the hosts, Lincoln City managed to navigate the storm and secure all three points when the final whistle echoed around the stadium."
