      "description": "Watch Bolton Wanderers vs Preston North End highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 16, 2026. On August 16, 2026, Bolton Wanderers and Preston North End locked horns in a high-stakes Championship fixture that delivered drama until the very end. The match was a classic display of English football, characterized by physical duels and tactical shifts. Visitors Strike Early The contest began at a frantic pace, with the referee busy from the outset as Alistair McCann picked up a booking in the 13th minute. Preston capitalised on the early momentum just sixty seconds later when Sam Dalby found the back of the net to give the visitors an early lead. Preston North End continued to apply pressure and doubled their advantage in the 25th minute. John McAtee turned provider, setting up Thierry Gale for a composed finish. However, the first half wasn't without its challenges for the away side, as both Jordan Thompson and Pol Valentin received yellow cards as they fought to maintain their two-goal cushion heading into the break. Bolton’s Late Fightback The second half saw Bolton Wanderers emerge with renewed intent, though Josh Sheehan was cautioned early on as tempers flared. A series of tactical substitutions followed, with Bolton introducing Jusef Erabi in the 64th minute to bolster their attack. Preston also rotated their squad, bringing on fresh legs like Andrija Vukcevic and Kyliane Dong to see out the game. Bolton’s persistence eventually paid off in the 86th minute when Jusef Erabi clinicaly finished a chance created by Andrija Vukcevic , setting up a grandstand finish. Despite Chris Forino-Joseph receiving a late yellow card and Bolton throwing everything forward in stoppage time, Preston held firm to secure a 2-1 victory."
